'' THE '.res' A '.rc' COMPILES TO IS NAMED AFTER THE OUTPUT, as every intermediate is. It
'' was '<stem>.res' beside the '.rc', so a '.res' of the user's own of that name was
'' overwritten and then deleted with the build's temporaries (audit F-74, CG-16).
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' CLEAN: build/.rc-own
'' COPY: tests/driver/src/res.rc => build/.rc-own/res.rc
'' COPY: tests/driver/src/res.bas => build/.rc-own/res.bas
'' WRITE: build/.rc-own/res.res :: USERS OWN
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 build/.rc-own/res.bas build/.rc-own/res.rc -o build/.rc-own/res.exe
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.rc-own/res.res :: USERS OWN
'' EXPECT-NO-FILE: build/.rc-own/res.exe.rc1.res
